<body>

<div class="container">
    <header>
        <h1>Bodice Block Drafting Guide</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">Complete technical reference for drafting Back and Front Bodice Pattern Blocks (Imperial & Metric)</p>
    </header>

    <section id="prerequisites">
        <h2>🛠️ Prerequisites & Setup</h2>
        <h3>Requirements & Tools</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Pattern paper, long ruler, L-square, French curve, and 2H pencil.</li>
            <li>All body measurements should be taken accurately over standard undergarments.</li>
            <li>Standard formulas use a baseline reference of <strong>UK Size 12 / 34" (87 cm) Bust</strong>.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Drafting Corrections & Adjustments</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Frame Width Adjustment:</strong> Add an extra <strong>2" (5 cm)</strong> to the initial frame width calculation to prevent front and back pattern overlaps on paper.</li>
            <li><strong>Nape Line Scaling:</strong> The Nape line drops for larger sizes and raises for smaller sizes (+/- 3/16" or 0.5 cm per 2 sizes). For a 38" (97 cm) bust, measure down 1 3/16" (3 cm) from the top line.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="measurements">
        <h2>📐 Reference Measurement Table</h2>
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Measurement Variable</th>
                    <th>Description / How to Measure</th>
                    <th>Baseline (UK 12 / 34" Bust)</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Bust</strong></td>
                    <td>Fullest part of the chest horizontally</td>
                    <td>34" (87 cm)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Waist</strong></td>
                    <td>Natural narrowest waistline</td>
                    <td>Standard proportion</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Hip</strong></td>
                    <td>Maximum hip level (8.25"–9" / 21–23 cm below waist)</td>
                    <td>Standard proportion</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Back Waist</strong></td>
                    <td>Nape of neck to natural waistline vertically</td>
                    <td>Standard proportion</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Waist to Hip</strong></td>
                    <td>Vertical distance from waist to maximum hip level</td>
                    <td>8.25"–9" (21–23 cm)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Chest Width</strong></td>
                    <td>Horizontal width across upper front chest</td>
                    <td>Standard proportion</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Back Width</strong></td>
                    <td>Horizontal width across upper back</td>
                    <td>Standard proportion</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </section>

    <section id="frame-setup">
        <h2>✏️ Part 1: Initial Frame Setup</h2>
        <p>Draw the primary bounding box frame to contain both back and front bodice drafts side-by-side.</p>
        <pre>
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+ Top Line
| [Back Block Frame]                          [Front Block Frame]       |
| CB                                                                 CF |
|                                                                       |
|                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+ Hip Line
        </pre>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Frame Width:</strong> Calculate Half Hip + 1.25" (3 cm) + <strong>2" (5 cm correction to prevent overlap)</strong>.</li>
            <li><strong>Frame Length:</strong> Calculate Back Waist + Waist-to-Hip + 1" (2.5 cm) <em>(add slightly more for larger sizes)</em>.</li>
            <li><strong>Key Guidelines & Labels:</strong>
                <ul>
                    <li>Left vertical boundary = <strong>CB (Center Back)</strong></li>
                    <li>Right vertical boundary = <strong>CF (Center Front)</strong></li>
                    <li>Bottom horizontal line = <strong>Hip Line</strong></li>
                </ul>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="back-bodice">
        <h2>📐 Part 2: Back Bodice Block</h2>
        <pre>
CB
+---[Nape Line]--------------------------------------
|     \ (Back Neck Curve)
|      +--[Shoulder Point]
|        |         +--[Across Back Line]
|           |            +--[Back Underarm Point]
|               |
|               |
+---[Waistline]--------------------------------------
|               |
+---[Hip Line]--+ [Back Hip Point]
        </pre>

        <h3>1. Guideline Construction</h3>
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Line Name</th>
                    <th>Vertical Measurement / Calculation</th>
                    <th>Action</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Nape Line</strong></td>
                    <td>Measure down <strong>1" (2.5 cm)</strong> from Top Line at CB. <em>(Adjust +/- 3/16" or 0.5 cm per 2 sizes)</em>.</td>
                    <td>Square across ~3" (8 cm).</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Waistline</strong></td>
                    <td>Measure down from Nape Line using full <strong>Back Waist</strong> length.</td>
                    <td>Square across to CF.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Bust Line</strong></td>
                    <td>Measure down from Nape Line: Half Back Waist + 3/8" (1 cm). <em>(For Bust > 40"/100 cm, use + 5/8" / 1.5 cm)</em>.</td>
                    <td>Square across to CF. <em>(Acts as armhole depth)</em>.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Shoulder Line</strong></td>
                    <td>Measure down <strong>1.25" (3 cm)</strong> from Nape Line.</td>
                    <td>Square across ~10" (25 cm).</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Across Back Line</strong></td>
                    <td>Find midpoint between <strong>Shoulder Line</strong> and <strong>Bust Line</strong>.</td>
                    <td>Square across guideline.</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <h3>2. Back Neckline & Shoulder</h3>
        <p><strong>Back Neck Width Formula:</strong></p>
        <div class="formula">
            Back Neck Width = ((Bust / 8) + 1.25" (3 cm)) / 2  [Alternative: Neck Size / 5]
        </div>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Back Neck Point:</strong> Measure along Nape Line by calculated neck width, then square up <strong>0.75" (2 cm)</strong>.</li>
            <li><strong>Neckline Curve:</strong> Draw a shallow curve flattening horizontally at CB.</li>
            <li><strong>Armhole Guideline:</strong> On Across Back Line, measure out (Half Back Width + 1/4" / 0.5 cm). Square down to Bust Line and up to Shoulder Line.</li>
            <li><strong>Back Shoulder Point:</strong> From Back Neck Point, extend a line equal to (Shoulder Length + 3/8" / 1 cm) to touch the Shoulder Line.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3>3. Back Armhole & Side Seam</h3>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Back Underarm Point:</strong> Extend armhole guide out <strong>2" (5 cm)</strong> at Bust Line <em>(up to 2.5" / 6.5 cm for larger sizes)</em>.</li>
            <li><strong>Corner Diagonal Guide:</strong> At the intersection of armhole guide and Bust Line, draw a 45° diagonal line and mark <strong>1.25" (3 cm)</strong> <em>(less for small, up to 1 5/8" / 4 cm for large)</em>.</li>
            <li><strong>Armhole Curve:</strong> Connect Shoulder Point through Across Back line (flattening for ~1.25" / 3 cm) and diagonal guide down to Back Underarm Point.</li>
            <li><strong>Shoulder Dart:</strong>
                <ul>
                    <li>Find midpoint of back shoulder line.</li>
                    <li>Draw guideline down 2.5" (6 cm), offset 3/8" (1 cm) left.</li>
                    <li>Draw dart legs 1/4" (0.5 cm) on either side of midpoint (Total Dart Width = 1/2" / 1 cm).</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li><strong>Provisional Side Seam:</strong> Mark <strong>Back Hip Point</strong> on Hip Line (Quarter Hip from CB). Connect Back Underarm Point to Back Hip Point with a straight line.</li>
        </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="front-bodice">
        <h2>📐 Part 3: Front Bodice Block</h2>
        <pre>
                                               CF
   [Front Shoulder Point]--+ (Bust Dart)      |
                           \                  |
                   [Chest Point]--+           |
                                   \          |
                        [Underarm Point]      |
                                   |          |
+----------------------------------+          | [Waistline]
                                   |          |
+----------------------------------+----------+ [Hip Line]
                             [Front Hip Point]
        </pre>

        <h3>1. Front Neckline & Shoulder</h3>
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Step</th>
                    <th>Measurement / Instruction</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Front Neck Width</strong></td>
                    <td>Back Neck Width - 1/4" (0.5 cm). Mark from CF along Top Line (<strong>Front Neck Point</strong>).</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Base of Neck</strong></td>
                    <td>Measure down CF <strong>3" (7.5 cm)</strong> from Top Line <em>(Range: 2.75" / 7 cm small to 3 3/8" / 8.5 cm large)</em>.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Neck Curve</strong></td>
                    <td>Square lines from Front Neck Point and Base of Neck. Draw 45° line at angle, mark <strong>1.25" (3 cm)</strong>, and curve smooth neckline.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Provisional Shoulder</strong></td>
                    <td>From CF along Top Line, measure <strong>6.5" (16.5 cm)</strong> and square down <strong>1.75" (4.5 cm)</strong>. Draw line from Front Neck Point through this mark.</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <h3>2. Bust Dart Construction</h3>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Dart Position Line:</strong> From CF, measure out <strong>Quarter Chest Width</strong>. Draw vertical line parallel to CF up to shoulder line and down <strong>1" (2.5 cm) below Bust Line</strong> (Bust Dart Point).</li>
            <li><strong>Dart Leg 1:</strong> From intersection on shoulder, measure <strong>0.75" (2 cm)</strong> left along shoulder line. Connect to Bust Dart Point.</li>
            <li><strong>Dart Leg 2:</strong> From Leg 1, measure <strong>Dart Width</strong> along shoulder line and draw to Bust Dart Point.
                <ul>
                    <li><em>Standard Small Bust Dart Width:</em> <strong>2.25" (5.5 cm) to 2.36" (6 cm)</strong>.</li>
                    <li><em>Large Bust:</em> Up to <strong>4" (10 cm)</strong>.</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li><strong>Front Shoulder Point:</strong> Mark full shoulder length starting from Front Neck Point, adding the dart width along the line.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3>3. Chest, Armhole & Side Seam</h3>
        <p><strong>Front Underarm Position Formula:</strong></p>
        <div class="formula">
            Front Underarm Distance from CF = Half Bust - Back Armhole Width (CB to Back Armhole Guide)
        </div>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Chest Line:</strong> Measure distance from Base of Neck to Bust Line. Divide by 3, measure that distance <strong>up</strong> from Bust Line, and square across.</li>
            <li><strong>Chest Point:</strong> Measure along Chest Line: (Half Chest Width + Dart Width at this level).</li>
            <li><strong>Front Underarm Point:</strong> Calculated via formula above (allows ~4" / 10 cm bust ease).</li>
            <li><strong>Armhole Curve:</strong>
                <ul>
                    <li>Join Shoulder Point to Chest Point. At midpoint, square inward <strong>3/8" (1 cm)</strong> toward CF.</li>
                    <li>From corner angle below Chest Point on Bust Line, draw a 45° diagonal guide of <strong>0.5" (1.5 cm)</strong> <em>(up to 1" / 2.5 cm for large)</em>.</li>
                    <li>Draw smooth curve passing through Shoulder Point, 3/8" mark, Chest Point, 45° guide, dropping slightly below Bust Line to join Front Underarm Point.</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li><strong>Front Hip Point & Side Seam:</strong> From CF along Hip Line, mark (Quarter Hip + 1.25" / 3 cm). Connect Front Underarm Point to Front Hip Point with a straight line.</li>
            <li><strong>True Bust Line:</strong> Draw line <strong>2" (4 cm) below Bust Line</strong> across to CB. Mark true <strong>Bust Point</strong> aligned vertically with the bust dart.</li>
        </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="checklist">
        <h2>📋 Checklist for Completed Blocks</h2>
        <ul class="checklist">
            <li>Frame includes 2" (5 cm) extra spacing to prevent center overlap.</li>
            <li>Nape line correctly adjusted for size profile.</li>
            <li>Shallow curve drafted for back neckline; deep 45° guided curve for front neckline.</li>
            <li>Back shoulder dart (1/2" / 1 cm width) placed at shoulder midpoint.</li>
            <li>Front bust dart aligned with Quarter Chest Width line and ending 1" below bust line.</li>
            <li>Armholes curved smoothly using respective 45° corner diagonal guidelines.</li>
            <li>Provisional side seams joined straight to calculated hip points.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>

</body>
